fferings were cut back in size in Q3 2026. Pellham Power, the largest utility buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, pulled its C$2.4B offering on 14 October. This is the strongest evidence that the window is shut or very selective (source: pellham-offering, the Q3 2026 equity issuance tracker).\n- **Consequence for capex:** Pellham said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender. Pellham is therefore adjusting its capex to the failed raise instead of finding other funding. That also suggests equity was a material part of its plan.\n- **Capex plans:** Pellham and Norvane filed their 2027 capital plans in October, mostly for substations and transformers (source: utility-capex-2027). The document doesn't give the amounts. They sit in a tender calendar I didn't retrieve.\n\nWhat I couldn't establish, because the corpus has no data on it:\n- Total equity needs per utility.\n- Valuation multiples and the discount to book or peers.\n- The dilution implied by the C$2.4B raise, because I have no market cap.\n- Sector index performance. The only related series is `utility_spreads` (bond spreads), which I didn't pull. It belongs to the debt-side nodes (n3 and n5).\n\n**Implication:** Don't assume equity covers 2027. Expect delayed or downsized raises, with more reliance on debt, hybrids or deferred capex. Pellham's ~40% cut in transformer orders is the clearest sign of this. Confidence is moderate on the direction and low on the sizing.","ttft_ms":3649,"type":"result","duration_ms":23094,"uuid":"1977d0eb-ab86-4d03-9bce-247df84a6424","ttft_stream_ms":2287,"time_to_request_ms":67,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":14,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":1,